From 3fc5adb9b39bdd55865dd56de4c5e32b5ed4c516 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <dev@example.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:47:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix EN/RU export & API locale bugs; add voivodeship-level
 regional pricing

- exports.py: PDF/Excel/Word were hardcoded to Polish labels regardless of
  the selected site language. Now locale-aware via app.i18n.t(), same as
  the web page already was.
- routes.py: /api/estimate hardcoded locale="pl" for the AI summary,
  ignoring the caller's actual ?lang/session locale. Now uses the real
  locale, matching the web form's behavior.
- llm.py: free-text parsing prompt only mentioned Polish/Ukrainian even
  though the UI supports EN/RU too; broadened it.
- New app/regions_data.py: single source of truth for 16 voivodeships,
  each split into capital city vs. voivodeship average (32 regions +
  1 national fallback = 33 total), with PL/EN/RU display names. Deliberately
  NOT split down to powiat (district) level -- that's ~380 districts with
  no reliable free data source behind it, and real PL kosztorys tools
  (Sekocenbud included) don't go that granular either; voivodeship +
  capital city is the actual professional-grade split.
- models.py: RegionalCoefficient gains voivodeship_code + is_capital for
  grouping the new picker.
- seed.py: seeds all 33 regions; ensure_regions() upgrades an
  already-seeded dev DB the same way ensure_extended_catalog() already
  does for the work catalog -- idempotent, never overwrites a coefficient
  that already exists (so a manually-tuned prod value survives an upgrade).
- templates/index.html: region <select> now renders <optgroup> per
  voivodeship with two options each (capital / average), plus the
  national-average fallback as a plain top-level option.
- Coefficients are a calibrated STARTING approximation grounded in
  publicly reported PL regional labor-cost spreads (Warsaw highest,
  eastern voivodeships lowest) -- same placeholder status as the rest of
  this project's pricing per data/README.md. Replace with real Sekocenbud
  regional data before quoting real clients on it.
- Tests: tests/test_regions.py (seeding, ordering, price scaling by
  region, dropdown rendering, upgrade idempotency) + regression tests in
  test_api.py/test_llm.py for both locale bugs.
